Mediocre Hacker schrieb:
> 
> I have a couple of questions for all you Nethack Luminaries:

Eh, i wouldn't consider myself very bright, but i'll try my best.

> First my character:
> 
> Ambience is a XP11 Elven (female) Wizard. HP:86; PW:105; AC:-4
> 
> Weapons:
> 
> a blessed elven dagger (in hand) and 19 uncursed daggers (in quiver)

No artefacts gained so far? Are you ever close to running out of ammo?
If no, you could downsize your dagger stack. Their usefulness depends
on your dagger skill, of course, and on your selection of spells and
wands; if you have some good offensive spells, they should be the
preferred attack when you really want to get something killed fast.
Wand and spell of sleep are also very neat.

> Armor:
> 
> (all +0, sigh) dwarvish iron helm, studded leather armor, burnt cloak
> of MR, elven boots, and leather gloves

Not spectacular, but o.k. for your current level.

> Rings: +3 and +1 ring of protection
>
> Pets: Master Lich named Lipton (formerly a cat) and a big dog named
> Cakes.
> 
> I have completed Sokuban and the Gnomish Mines and wonder what to do
> next. I have a lot of gold from a couple of Leprecaun (sp?) rooms and
> will be heading to visit the co-aligned priest in minetown for a
> couple of doses of AC and maybe some saccing.

Both of them very good ideas. Getting a special weapon would help
quite a bit. And getting some more protection would make your life a
lot safer.

> Here are my questions (problems):
> 
> Lipton kills shopkeepers and will try to kill the priest (I would
> guess).

Correct. Your pets will attack nearly anything that's not higher-level
than them; and there isn't much of higher level than master and arch
liches. The priest will probably last two to three turns. And the ways
of keeping the lich from harming the cleric are either staying away
from the temple or keeping the lich off the level while you do your
donating and sacrificing. And while it's on another level, its
tameness will decrease...

> I am worried about him going feral if I leave him behind, but
> he is so handy for killing all but cold resistant things.

Liches of any kind don't eat (i.e., their tameness cannot be
increased) and the major liches are almost immune to charming. A major
lich is not likely to stay tame throughout the game, and it can cause
massive havoc when it goes feral; i usually "dump" a pet lich
somewhere out of harm's way after a while, unless i can polymorph it
into something more manageable.

> What to do,
> what to do? I thought about abandoning him in Sokuban.

Might be a good idea to do this soon, unless you want to have some
priests killed.

> Food is a problem. Usually by this time I have a stack or two of food
> items, but since I am wearing those two rings, consumption has
> increased to the point where I have no food to speak of.

AFAIK, rings of protection are just ordinary rings - i.e. they should
increase food consumption by no more than 10%. To really solve food
troubles, it'd be best to dive to somewhere with enough large
monsters, so you can "live off the land". Might be best not to bother
very much with sacrificing right now - just buy some protection and do
some exploring (a spell of create monster would of course help solving
food troubles).

If all else fails, kick a sink for a while to get a black pudding,
then split it up a bit (you'll need a metal weapon for this) and eat
the corpses; watch your hitpoints before eating, though. You can only
harvest one pudding per sink, but one pudding can provide a lot of
nourishment if you clone it a bit.

> What to do,
> what to do? Take off the +1 ring for a while? Both rings?

The +1 is hardly worth wearing. If you have two more points of
protection, it might be reasonable to dump this ring, perhaps in
favour of another ring.

> Where should I go to beef up my AC? (After the priest)

Barracks, if you can find any. Do you have reflection? If yes, Ludios
should become attractive; and there are tons of armour there, you can
practically expect to get enchanted stuff for every equipment slot.

